{"id": "sfmta-garage-contracts-counted-by-fee", "title": "Muni’s garage contracts counted only the fee: $231 million spent before the Board saw them", "seconds": 130.4, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.029, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "8ad69cbfdf3fa9b4", "words": 399, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["sources", "established[0]"], "text": "February 2022. The Board’s analyst opens four of Muni’s garage contracts.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.79, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bla", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 2 February 2022", "text": "SFMTA garage management contracts, Files 22-0004 to 22-0007", "mark": "garage management"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.5, 0.76, 1.8, 1.95, 2.25, 2.65, 2.98, 3.23, 3.32, 3.65, 4.03]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Since 2012, private operators have run 20 public garages for the agency.", "t0": 4.91, "t1": 9.24, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "20 public garages", "kicker": "Private operators", "sub": "a monthly fee, plus every cost reimbursed"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.54, 1.22, 1.61, 2.08, 2.21, 2.43, 2.76, 3.08, 3.55, 3.67, 3.8]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Each gets a monthly fee, and all its costs reimbursed.", "t0": 9.36, "t1": 12.15, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "20 public garages", "kicker": "Private operators", "sub": "a monthly fee, plus every cost reimbursed"}, "emph": ["all its costs"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.45, 0.53, 0.88, 1.24, 1.43, 1.61, 1.78, 2.14]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "How much did the four contracts pay out, by January 2022?", "t0": 12.27, "t1": 16.45, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Four garage contracts", "sub": "February 2012 to January 2022"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.39, 0.51, 0.63, 0.86, 1.37, 1.61, 2.13, 2.33, 2.85, 3.1]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "231,349,383 dollars.", "t0": 16.45, "t1": 19.31, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$231,349,383", "label": "paid out under four SFMTA garage contracts", "sub": "February 2012 to January 2022"}, "emph": ["231,349,383"], "wt": [0.04, 0.38, 0.6, 0.89, 1.48, 1.75, 2.07, 2.44]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "In December 2011, each garage-group contract was set at its fees alone:", "t0": 19.93, "t1": 24.65, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Group A, B and C garages", "kicker": "December 2011", "sub": "management fees only", "chip": "$907,920"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.56, 0.84, 1.44, 1.67, 2.32, 2.85, 2.98, 3.2, 3.29, 3.44, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "907,920 dollars.", "t0": 24.65, "t1": 27.25, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Group A, B and C garages", "kicker": "December 2011", "sub": "management fees only", "chip": "$907,920"}, "emph": ["907,920"], "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.62, 0.93, 1.36, 1.6, 1.89, 2.19]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[1]"], "text": "The 5th and Mission Garage, 587,510. Reimbursed costs were left out.", "t0": 27.67, "t1": 33.82, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["5th and Mission Garage", "$587,510"], "b": ["the operators’ costs", "left out"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["left out"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.43, 0.53, 0.8, 1.64, 1.94, 2.2, 2.78, 3.18, 3.45, 3.71, 4.56, 5.13, 5.48, 5.64, 5.9]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "And of everything paid out, how much was fees?", "t0": 33.94, "t1": 37.07, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Of $231,349,383 paid out", "sub": "how much was fees?"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.38, 0.82, 1.1, 1.63, 1.87, 2.15, 2.34]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "4,578,205 dollars. The rest was reimbursed costs.", "t0": 37.07, "t1": 40.95, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$4,578,205", "label": "management fees, 2012 to January 2022", "sub": "the rest: reimbursed costs"}, "emph": ["4,578,205"], "wt": [0.04, 0.41, 0.65, 0.91, 1.16, 1.46, 2.26, 2.45, 2.72, 2.92, 3.45]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[1]"], "text": "Why does it matter? The Charter sends any contract of 10 million or more to the Board.", "t0": 41.37, "t1": 45.51, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Charter section 9.118(b) sends any contract of $10 million or more to the Board of Supervisors.", "kicker": "The Board line"}, "emph": ["10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.32, 0.43, 1.03, 1.19, 1.55, 1.82, 2.02, 2.51, 2.62, 2.86, 3.21, 3.33, 3.57, 3.66, 3.77]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Counting only the fee kept each contract under that line for ten years.", "t0": 45.63, "t1": 49.08, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Charter section 9.118(b) sends any contract of $10 million or more to the Board of Supervisors.", "kicker": "The Board line"}, "emph": ["only the fee"], "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.56, 0.69, 1.0, 1.27, 1.47, 2.04, 2.24, 2.43, 2.7, 2.85, 3.09]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Each contract’s spending passed 10 million dollars by fiscal 2014-15.", "t0": 49.3, "t1": 53.45, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2012-02-01", "to": "2022-02-25", "days": null, "fromLab": "contracts begin", "toLab": "first Board vote", "kicker": "Over the Board line"}, "emph": ["10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.74, 1.15, 1.42, 1.63, 1.95, 2.27, 2.45, 2.84, 3.11, 3.57, 3.67]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "timeline[6]"], "text": "So when did the Board of Supervisors first vote on them?", "t0": 53.57, "t1": 56.75, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2012-02-01", "to": "2022-02-25", "days": null, "fromLab": "contracts begin", "toLab": "first Board vote", "kicker": "Over the Board line"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.41, 0.55, 0.67, 0.91, 1.0, 1.71, 2.0, 2.24, 2.35]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "timeline[6]"], "text": "February 2022, retroactively.", "t0": 56.75, "t1": 59.15, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "25 February 2022", "label": "first Board vote, retroactive", "sub": "Resolutions 055-22 to 058-22"}, "emph": ["retroactively"], "wt": [0.04, 0.59, 0.86, 1.51]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "It came to the Board only because the agency asked to extend the contracts a year.", "t0": 59.57, "t1": 63.34, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "A one-year extension", "kicker": "January 2022", "sub": "the agency’s request to the Board"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.35, 0.45, 0.56, 0.84, 1.06, 1.35, 1.49, 1.94, 2.15, 2.3, 2.72, 2.83, 3.36, 3.45]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Why only the fee, in 2011? The agency and the City Attorney found no record explaining it.", "t0": 63.56, "t1": 68.96, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "SFMTA and City Attorney staff “were unable to locate records explaining why the contract amounts only referenced the management fees”.", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, footnote 7"}, "emph": ["no record"], "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.53, 0.69, 1.12, 1.3, 1.64, 2.52, 2.71, 3.12, 3.22, 3.32, 3.59, 4.0, 4.27, 4.47, 4.78, 5.29]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]"], "text": "The agency’s letter to the Board calls it a “regrettable error”.", "t0": 69.08, "t1": 72.07, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Staff recognizes this regrettable error", "kicker": "SFMTA letter, 21 January 2022"}, "emph": ["regrettable error"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.63, 0.87, 0.98, 1.1, 1.44, 1.75, 1.87, 1.96, 2.63]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The committee asked for a review of all its contracts, within 60 days.", "t0": 72.29, "t1": 75.86, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Review all SFMTA contracts", "kicker": "2 February 2022", "sub": "report within 60 days"}, "emph": ["all its contracts"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.54, 0.74, 0.86, 0.93, 1.25, 1.36, 1.53, 1.69, 2.42, 2.76, 3.13]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "A report dated September 2022 is listed on the file.", "t0": 75.98, "t1": 79.18, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "rpt", "kicker": "Attachment to Board File 220004", "text": "SFMTA Report 092822", "mark": "092822"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.53, 0.82, 1.31, 1.61, 2.15, 2.28, 2.6, 2.71, 2.81]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "What it found is not in the records we hold.", "t0": 79.3, "t1": 81.33, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "rpt", "kicker": "Attachment to Board File 220004", "text": "SFMTA Report 092822", "mark": "092822"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.29, 0.61, 0.77, 0.97, 1.06, 1.21, 1.56, 1.7]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[5]", "timeline[3]"], "text": "The agency’s own resolutions data skips the garage extensions of October 2021.", "t0": 81.45, "t1": 86.01, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "SFMTA Board resolutions", "kicker": "DataSF v5uc-gana", "sub": "the garage extensions of 5 October 2021: absent"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.65, 0.84, 1.5, 1.8, 2.09, 2.21, 2.58, 3.11, 3.22, 3.66, 3.96]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "The 2010 bid rules let no firm hold more than one garage group.", "t0": 86.23, "t1": 89.71, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "One group per firm", "sub": "2010 request for proposals"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Imperial Parking", "sub": "disqualified; senior partner of IMCO"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Pacific Park Management", "sub": "bought by Imperial, 2014"}], "kicker": "One-award rule"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.44, 0.71, 0.97, 1.29, 1.52, 1.73, 2.04, 2.29, 2.46, 2.65, 2.84, 3.23]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "Imperial Parking, IMCO’s senior partner, was disqualified on that ground.", "t0": 89.83, "t1": 93.98, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "One group per firm", "sub": "2010 request for proposals"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Imperial Parking", "sub": "disqualified; senior partner of IMCO"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Pacific Park Management", "sub": "bought by Imperial, 2014"}], "kicker": "One-award rule"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 1.14, 1.67, 2.03, 2.56, 2.75, 3.49, 3.62, 3.79]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[4]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "In 2014, it bought Pacific Park Management, and took over Group A.", "t0": 94.1, "t1": 98.26, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Group A", "kicker": "2014", "sub": "assigned to Imperial Parking"}, "emph": ["Group A"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.48, 1.23, 1.4, 1.65, 2.09, 2.35, 2.96, 3.16, 3.41, 3.65, 3.97]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "timeline[8]"], "text": "Since February 2023, IMCO and LAZ manage all 21 garages and lots.", "t0": 98.38, "t1": 103.34, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["IMCO Parking", "$219 million"], "b": ["LAZ Parking", "$189 million"], "kicker": "All 21 garages and lots, since February 2023", "arrows": false}, "emph": ["all 21"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.71, 1.0, 1.86, 2.42, 2.61, 3.02, 3.32, 3.49, 3.96, 4.44, 4.56]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[7]", "established[8]"], "text": "The agency’s resolutions approved fee-only amounts in October. The analyst dated approval to December.", "t0": 103.56, "t1": 108.91, "shot": "record-7,8-5 October 2021", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bd25a", "text": "5 October 2021", "mark": "5 October 2021", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.65, 1.29, 1.65, 2.12, 2.47, 2.59, 3.45, 3.63, 4.03, 4.31, 4.74, 4.85]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "The garages earn far more than they cost: 620 million dollars of revenue.", "t0": 109.13, "t1": 113.71, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["revenue to January 2022", "$620 million"], "b": ["spent", "$231 million"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["620 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.65, 0.88, 1.17, 1.38, 1.51, 1.67, 2.41, 2.68, 2.98, 3.32, 3.7, 4.04, 4.14]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "The question is ten years of spending with no Board vote.", "t0": 113.83, "t1": 116.23, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["revenue to January 2022", "$620 million"], "b": ["spent", "$231 million"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["no Board vote"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.49, 0.61, 0.82, 1.05, 1.13, 1.52, 1.69, 1.86, 2.14]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[2]", "notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Nothing here says any operator was paid for work not done.", "t0": 116.35, "t1": 119.2, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Why only the fee was counted", "What the September 2022 report found", "That any operator was paid for costs it did not incur"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.52, 0.77, 0.99, 1.44, 1.6, 1.84, 2.0, 2.27, 2.5]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The September 2022 report, and the 2011 staff report.", "t0": 119.32, "t1": 124.69, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "SFMTA Report 092822: the review of all SFMTA contracts"}, {"who": "", "what": "The 2011 staff report that set the $907,920 amounts"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.34, 0.63, 1.19, 1.35, 1.83, 2.12, 2.6, 3.37, 3.62, 3.73, 3.96, 4.37, 4.72, 5.03]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has said why only the fee was counted.", "t0": 124.81, "t1": 127.3, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.67, 0.79, 1.03, 1.32, 1.56, 1.7, 1.91, 2.09]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.42, "t1": 129.48, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.61, 0.77, 1.0, 1.08, 1.18, 1.42, 1.7]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The finding", "lead1": "Only the fee", "lead2": "Past the line", "lead3": "No record", "lead4": "The review", "lead5": "One rule, one owner", "close": "Where it stands", "record": "The public record"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "document"}